        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(voice-call): unref ngrok startup timeout and mark closed on timeout",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`startNgrokTunnel`'s 30s startup `setTimeout` was never `unref()`'d, so an abandoned tunnel promise kept the host process alive until the timer fired. On the timeout path the child was killed but `closed` was not set, leaving the `stop()` cleanup path inconsistent with the eventual `close` event.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`unref()` the startup timer so it cannot pin the event loop, and mark the process `closed` on timeout so `stop()` does not try to re-kill an already-terminating child.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe voice-call tunnel startup no longer holds the process open when its caller has moved on; no change to successful tunnel startup.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression test \"unrefs the ngrok startup timeout so it cannot keep the host process alive\": spies on `setTimeout` and asserts the returned timer's `unref()` is called. **Red before the fix** (`unref` called 0 times), green after.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/voice-call/src/tunnel.test.ts` → 16 passed.\n- Verified `upstream/main` is byte-identical for this region (not yet fixed), so this PR is not a duplicate.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed: `startNgrokTunnel` in `extensions/voice-call/src/tunnel.ts` started a 30s ngrok-startup timeout with `setTimeout` but never unref'd it, so the host process could be kept alive solely by the pending timer. The fix calls `timeout.unref()` and also marks the tunnel `closed` in the timeout branch before killing the process.\n\nReal environment tested: macOS 15, Node v24.18.0 (Homebrew node@24), vitest 4.1.9. The changed timer/unref path is driven through a mocked ngrok child process so the exact `unref()` call is asserted without spawning a real tunnel.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n- `npx vitest run extensions/voice-call/src/tunnel.test.ts`\n\nEvidence after fix (CI `Real behavior proof` job passed; local suite asserts):\n```\n- \"unrefs the ngrok startup timeout so it cannot keep the host process alive\" -> setTimeout's unref() called\n```\n\nObserved result after fix: The 30s startup watchdog no longer holds the event loop open, and the timeout branch now marks the tunnel closed before killing the process. The `Real behavior proof` CI check passed for this head.\n\nWhat was not tested: A real ngrok subprocess and live tunnel was not started (ngrok is fully mocked); the proof targets the exact changed lines — `timeout.unref()` and the `closed` flag in the timeout branch — which are process/timer-control contracts.\n",
        "branch": "fix/voice-call-tunnel-unref",
